[10.575723, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[10.604492, "o", "\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K   R1  workload identity tsg-helpdesk is shared by tickets, mail: logs can't tell them apart\r\n            why: AgentCore: create separate workload identities with separate IAM roles (scope-credential-provider-access)\r\n\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K   R2  IAM role tsg-agent-helpdesk is shared by tickets, mail: each gets the other's permissions\r\n            why: same page; OWASP NHI9:2025 NHI Reuse\r\n\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K   R4  launcher takes the user from request-body: anyone can claim to be anyone\r\n            why: AgentCore: prefer GetWorkloadAccessTokenForJWT; derive the userId from the authenticated principal\r\n\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K   R5  role tsg-agent-helpdesk can be assumed without a SourceIdentity: CloudTrail won't name the human\r\n            why: IAM: source identity is logged in CloudTrail and persists across role chaining\r\n\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K   R7  role tsg-agent-helpdesk: bedrock-agentcore:GetWorkloadAccessToken*, bedrock-agentcore:GetResourceOauth2Token on Resource \"*\" can use every credential provider\r\n            why: AgentCore: the service does not enforce additional binding between workload identities and credential providers\r\n\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K   R8  role tsg-agent-helpdesk doesn't deny GetWorkloadAccessTokenForUserId (an unverified user ID)\r\n            why: AgentCore: explicitly deny GetWorkloadAccessTokenForUserId where a JWT is always available\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[K--\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n6 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K, 5 MEDIUM, 0 LOW  (11 findings)\r\n"]
